@namespace Fravashi.Web.Components.Settings.Framework

@* Honesty banner for the Framework tab (backlog 80). Archived ADR 0005 deferred the projection engine when framework
   artifacts moved into the database, so every kind authored here is stored and NOTHING reads those rows back
   into an agent session. Until backlog 69 builds the projection, the tab must say so where the authoring
   happens, rather than let a user configure a framework and believe it took effect.

   Reuses the studio's existing `.ob-warning` message convention (studio.css, the same look the onboarding
   steps use for a plainly stated caveat); it is a global class, not an onboarding-scoped one. Deliberately
   NOT dismissible: a dismissed banner would put the honesty gap one click away. Delete this component and its
   call site in FrameworkSection when 69 lands. *@

<div class="ob-warning framework-not-applied" role="note" data-testid="framework-not-applied">
    <strong>Stored, not applied yet.</strong>
    Skills, agents, commands, hooks, MCP servers and plugins authored here are saved in @(ProductName.Short)'s database,
    and nothing writes them into an agent session yet: a skill is not invocable, a subagent is not available,
    and a hook does not fire. Authoring now is safe, everything saved is kept, and it starts taking effect
    when the projection that applies these artifacts to sessions ships. That work is on the backlog.
</div>
